{
  "file": "ui-workbench.zh-CN.clif",
  "stratum": "ui",
  "notes": "Slatepath data workbench strings, written for CLARION-Core v0.3. Every item is labelled A to D in the first position of its tags: A decisive (the source alone cannot be translated correctly - the type tag, the page the context names or the width budget decides), B high-risk (systematic model bias: textbook jargon for default, cache, latency, resolution and throughput, Han-Latin spacing, numerals, the {name} placeholder, an ICU plural and an ICU select whose selector keys are engine values), C cross-entry (a term, a pronoun, a step number or an echoed verb that only resolves against other entries in this file), D normal text (ordinary workbench prose and labels that any competent translator should get right, kept as the baseline). Six minimal pairs share a source and a neutral id and differ on exactly one field: mode-01a/b and mode-04a/b on type (proper noun against common noun, label against sentence), term-02a/b and term-03a/b on context (the same word on two different pages), slot-05a/b and slot-06a/b on max-width (a wide menu against the narrow inspector rail). The term 'scratch table' occurs in the source of six entries and must be rendered the same way in all of them; the header states that requirement without naming the rendering, so the consistency has to come from the file itself. The file holds 32 entries: 12 A, 7 B, 5 C and 8 D. The product, its modules and its demo data set are invented and share nothing with the Harborline Console file in the same stratum.",
  "provenance": {
    "source": "original text written for CLARION",
    "url": "",
    "license": "CC0-1.0",
    "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/",
    "redistributable": true,
    "human_verified": false,
    "verifier": "",
    "retrieved": "2026-01-01",
    "origin": "original",
    "context_origin": "original",
    "notes": "Original text written for this benchmark, therefore free of training-data contamination. The workbench, its modules and its wording are invented and do not reproduce any shipping product interface."
  },
